{
 "request_id": "f22328acdd00",
 "question": "Compare high-bias and high-variance models using learning curves.",
 "answer": "High-bias models, as seen in their learning curves, show both training and validation errors are high and converge close to each other, indicating adding more data does not significantly help. [S1] High-variance models, as exemplified by deep decision trees, have a low training error and a large gap between training and validation errors, suggesting validation error continues to fall with more data, indicating more data helps.",
